title: A Volkspartei Again?
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/poster_0.jpg
view-if: peoples_party_support >= 3 and peoples_party = 0 and peoples_party_timer == 0
on-arrival: peoples_party_timer = 6
tags: party_affairs
max-visits: 4

= A Volkspartei Again?

Since Bad Godesberg in 1959, the SPD has seen itself as a people's party for all who work for a living. But at 16% in 2025, it is hard to call it a Volkspartei any longer. The industrial working class is shrinking, the educated middle class votes Grüne, and many workers now vote AfD.

Netzwerk Berlin and the Seeheimer Kreis want a new opening to the centre: to the self-employed, to the suburbs, to the countryside and to the East, with a programme that is less about the party's traditions and more about everyday problems. The Parlamentarische Linke and the AfA warn that the party would lose its soul and its last core voters.

- @support_peoples_party: Yes, we must become a big-tent party again!
- @build_support: We must build more support in the party first.
- @support_peoples_party_hard: Despite the opposition of the left and the AfA, we will open the party to the centre.
- @no_new_ideas: No, we must first win back our core voters.
- @root: Perhaps we can discuss this at a later time.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@build_support
view-if: (center_strength + reformist_strength < left_strength + labor_strength) or peoples_party_support < 5
on-arrival: peoples_party_support += 1; center_strength += 5; left_strength -= 5; left_dissent += 5

We push the idea in the party's commissions and regional associations, against the resistance of the left.

@support_peoples_party
choose-if: (center_strength + reformist_strength >= left_strength + labor_strength) and peoples_party_support >= 4
unavailable-subtitle: The opposition is too strong.
on-arrival: center_strength += 15; reformist_strength += 15; center_dissent -= 10; reformist_dissent -= 10; peoples_party = 1; workers_spd -= 6; rural_spd += 6; new_middle_spd += 6; old_middle_spd += 5; catholics_spd += 4; pensioners_spd += 2; left_dissent += 25; labor_dissent += 15; linke_relation -= 10; linke_coalition_dissent += 1; coalition_dissent -= 1; cdu_relation += 5*(1-dissent); fdp_relation += 5*(1-dissent)
achievement: volkspartei

A party congress adopts a new programme for a broad Social Democracy of the centre. The left calls it a second Agenda 2010, and some union leaders leave in protest. But the party is reaching voters it has not reached in years.

Should we run a campaign to present our new programme?

- @campaign_workers
- @campaign_middle
- @campaign_rural
- @campaign_unemployed
- @campaign_women
- @campaign_catholics

@support_peoples_party_hard
subtitle: This will increase dissent.
view-if: (center_strength + reformist_strength < left_strength + labor_strength) or (peoples_party_support < 4)
on-arrival: center_strength += 10; reformist_strength += 8; peoples_party = 1; workers_spd -= 8; rural_spd += 6; new_middle_spd += 6; old_middle_spd += 5; catholics_spd += 4; pensioners_spd += 2; left_dissent += 40; labor_dissent += 30; linke_relation -= 10; linke_coalition_dissent += 1; coalition_dissent -= 1
achievement: volkspartei

After a bitter fight, the leadership pushes the new programme through the party congress. The left calls it a second Agenda 2010. But the party is reaching voters it has not reached in years.

Should we run a campaign to present our new programme?

- @campaign_workers
- @campaign_middle
- @campaign_rural
- @campaign_unemployed
- @campaign_women
- @campaign_catholics

@campaign_workers
title: Campaign among workers, to ease their doubts about our changes.
on-arrival: workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent);

Workers are still the heart of our voters, and we must not lose them while we reach out to others.

@campaign_middle
title: Campaign among the middle classes.
on-arrival: old_middle_spd += 5*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 6*(1-dissent)

Employees, public servants and small business owners are listening to us again.

@campaign_rural
title: Campaign in small towns and the countryside.
choose-if: rural_policy > 0
unavailable-subtitle: We have not enacted any rural policies yet.
on-arrival: rural_spd += 7*(1-dissent)

With our rural policies to show, people in the countryside are more willing to listen.

@campaign_unemployed
title: Campaign among the unemployed.
on-arrival: unemployed_spd += 6*(1-dissent);

The unemployed and the working poor are still a key part of our voters.

@campaign_women
title: Campaign among women.
on-arrival: workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); rural_spd += 3*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 3*(1-dissent);

Women of every background are a majority of the electorate, and many of them vote for us.

@campaign_catholics
title: Campaign in the East.
on-arrival: catholics_spd += 6*(1-dissent);

Across the East, many people have given up on the old western parties. We send our best people to listen.

@no_new_ideas
on-arrival: center_strength -= 6; center_dissent += 5; labor_strength += 5; left_strength += 3; peoples_party = 0; peoples_party_support -= 3

Before we chase new voters, we must win back the ones we lost: the workers, the pensioners and the people in the old industrial regions.
